    PE-1296: Fix invalid thread filter SQL when SLA filter is empty (#11414)
    
    <!-- CURSOR_AGENT_PR_BODY_BEGIN -->
    Prod `core-graphql-api` has been erroring on `getThreads` with Postgres
    `syntax_error` (`syntax error at or near "AND"`) — Datadog Error
    Tracking issue
    [99a58b60-c265-11f1-bfbb-da7ad0900005](https://app.datadoghq.eu/error-tracking?issueId=99a58b60-c265-11f1-bfbb-da7ad0900005).
    
    The MCP `getThreads` operation always sends a `serviceLevelAgreements: {
    statuses, types }` block even when both variables are null.
    `buildFilters` still treated that input as active and the SLA filter
    builder returned an empty SQL fragment. Joining real predicates with
    that fragment produced invalid SQL like `"assigned_to" IS NOT NULL AND
    AND ("created_at" >= …)`.
    
    When no SLA (or agent status) criteria are set, those builders now
    return `ignoreFilter()` (`1 = 1`), matching `rangeFilter` and other
    no-op filters.
    
    Related: Linear PE-1296.
